  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="3abf-6265-2afc-5d3e" name="Armenian (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #25 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). The Armenian Satrapy of the Persian Empire became independent during the Successor wars, and remained so until divided between Rome and Sassanid Persia. This list reflects the army under Tigranes who fought unsuccessfully against the Romans. Allies: The army may have an allied contingent from the Seleucid list. However Seleucid units will fail their Allies and Mercenaries roll on a 1 or 2 and all reduce their leadership value by 1 (-1 point per figure).

ARMY COMPOSITION:
[Armenian]
  Cavalry: at least 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: At least 50% Infantry: Up to 25% Allies: Up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
